    <item>
      <title>The Eye Of The Storm | #FPL GW22</title>
      <description>The hectic festive period ends as we #fpl managers enter a period of transition between that and the fixture swing and incoming chip season to come as we come to the cusp of the business end to the #fantasyfootball season.

Tom &amp; Sam look over the potential forecast for the next little while, with Sam explaining the picture for chips and giving some possible dates and routes for us to consider.

And then it's looking at midfielders as many are seeking to move on the likes of Cunha and, perhaps, Foden or Saka - do you go expensive with Palmer or across to Bruno, or downswing elsewhere? Plus a range of other players in form Vs fixtures before your usual features and then a look at our teams.

If you haven't already, please like and subscribe to our feed.


Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Jan 2026 22:38:00 -0000</pubDate>
      <itunes:episodeType>full</itunes:episodeType>
      <itunes:author>Who Got The Assist?</itunes:author>
      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>The hectic festive period ends as we #fpl managers enter a period of transition between that and the fixture swing and incoming chip season to come as we come to the cusp of the business end to the #fantasyfootball season.

Tom &amp; Sam look over the potential forecast for the next little while, with Sam explaining the picture for chips and giving some possible dates and routes for us to consider.

And then it's looking at midfielders as many are seeking to move on the likes of Cunha and, perhaps, Foden or Saka - do you go expensive with Palmer or across to Bruno, or downswing elsewhere? Plus a range of other players in form Vs fixtures before your usual features and then a look at our teams.

If you haven't already, please like and subscribe to our feed.


Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</itunes:summary>
