    <item>
      <title>Midfield Meta Shift? | FPL Gameweek 9</title>
      <description>As FPL returned after international break, we’re here to assess the fallout as Haaland rolls on, Mateta bags a hattie (and could’ve had more) but others falter – and Ange is shown the door after just 39 days.

First we give a mention of the dawning Dyche era at Forest and its possible fantasy football ramifications, and then it’s on to our main topic this week: has the midfield actually disappointed as some are suggesting, or is it just that Semenyo’s ridiculous performance has distorted our perception?

And then in form vs fixtures, a focus on forwards and defenders – in particularly Palace and Chelsea assets, plus Big Nick Woltemade.

Plus finally one week punts, a best captain chat and perhaps a quiet week for our teams with Sam having just wildcarded and Tom desperately attempting to keep his knee in check.

If you enjoyed this, leave a 5-star review, say something nice if you’d like, and
do subscribe to our feed – we really appreciate it, and it helps us so much!
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
