    <item>
      <title>Double Trouble | Gameweek 26</title>
      <description>DGW25 failed to live up to many of our lofty expectations (what else is new), so the WGTA take a wider look at setting up for Double Gameweeks and how they can potentially act as distractions from the greater good (Hot Fuzz reference implied).

We look at the psychology of Outcome in FPL, and how that might temper how we view double gameweeks going forward.

Plus in the gameweek preview we look at the midfield prospects to replace Jota, Darwin replacements in the forward line (Solanke or Hojland?) and defenders (er, anyone?). And do we keep faith in Haaland as captain?

Please subscribe and leave a 5* review if you enjoy the show! 🙏
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
